# lostping

**AIS dark-vessel detection pipeline.**  
Ingests raw AIS CSVs, engineers maritime anomaly features, scores every vessel 0–100, and produces interactive maps + sortable HTML reports.

```
7.3 M pings · 4,621 vessels · 34 flagged · top vessel JET 1 scored 73.3
```

---

## Install

```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-org/lostping.git
cd lostping
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

Requires Python ≥ 3.10.

---

## Quick start

```bash
# Full pipeline — ingest → features → models → reports
lostping run --input ./data/ais/ --output ./out/

# Narrow to a region and raise the flag threshold
lostping run \
  --input   ./data/ais/ \
  --output  ./out/ \
  --region  gulf_of_mexico \
  --threshold 60

# Re-score without re-ingesting (fast iteration on model params)
lostping score --matrix ./out/features.parquet --output ./out/

# Rebuild the map from saved data
lostping map --pings ./out/pings.parquet --flagged ./out/flagged.json
```

Outputs land in `--output`:

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| `flagged.json` | Full event list per flagged vessel |
| `map.html` | Dark Folium map — coloured tracks, gap markers, loiter circles |
| `report.html` | Sortable dark-theme summary table |

---

## Pipeline

```
AIS CSVs
  └─ loader.py       chunk-read, region filter, column clean
  └─ cleaner.py      drop bad MMSIs / dupes / sparse tracks
        │
        ├─ gaps.py          AIS blackout detection + STS zone proximity
        ├─ trajectory.py    speed variance, heading erraticism, reversals
        └─ spatial.py       port loitering, open-ocean stops, EEZ hugging
              │
              └─ builder.py      join → one feature matrix per vessel
                    │
                    ├─ isolation.py   Isolation Forest per vessel type
                    ├─ loiter.py      DBSCAN — vessels orbiting a fixed point
                    └─ zscore.py      z-score each vessel against type peers
                          │
                          └─ scorer.py   combine → risk score 0–100 + reason string
                                │
                                ├─ json_report.py
                                ├─ map.py
                                └─ html_report.py
```

### Ingest

`loader.py` reads CSVs in configurable chunks (default 100 k rows), filters to a named region bounding box, and normalises column names.  
`cleaner.py` drops rows with invalid MMSIs (non-9-digit, reserved ranges), exact duplicates, and vessels with fewer than `--min-pings` position reports.

### Features

| Module | Signals |
|---|---|
| `gaps.py` | AIS blackout duration, blackout count, proximity to known STS transfer zones during gaps |
| `trajectory.py` | Speed variance, heading erraticism (circular std-dev), reversal count, impossible-speed events |
| `spatial.py` | Port loiter time, open-ocean stop count, EEZ boundary hugging distance |
| `builder.py` | Left-joins all three onto a single vessel-level feature matrix |

### Models

| Module | Method | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `isolation.py` | Isolation Forest | Multivariate outlier per vessel type |
| `loiter.py` | DBSCAN on lat/lon | Detects vessels orbiting a fixed location |
| `zscore.py` | Per-type z-score | Flags statistical outliers within peer group |
| `scorer.py` | Weighted sum | Combines all signals → `risk_score` ∈ [0, 100] + `reason` string |

Vessels above `--threshold` (default 50) are written to `flagged.json`.

### Reports

`map.py` builds a dark-background Folium map. Track colour encodes risk score (green → amber → red). Gap events are marked with circles; loiter clusters get filled rings.  
`html_report.py` renders a sortable table — click any column header to re-rank.

---

## CLI reference

```
lostping run [OPTIONS]

  --input,      -i   DIR or CSV   AIS data source (required)
  --output,     -o   DIR          Report destination  [./lostping_out]
  --region,     -r   NAME         Named region filter (e.g. gulf_of_mexico)
  --threshold,  -t   FLOAT        Flag threshold 0–100  [50]
  --chunk-size       INT          CSV rows per chunk  [100000]
  --min-pings        INT          Minimum pings to keep a track  [10]
  --sts-zones        PATH         STS zone GeoJSON (optional)
  --eez              PATH         EEZ boundary GeoJSON (optional)
  --verbose,    -v               Print full tracebacks on error

lostping score [OPTIONS]

  --matrix,     -m   PATH        features.parquet from a previous run (required)
  --output,     -o   DIR         [./lostping_out]
  --threshold,  -t   FLOAT       [50]

lostping map [OPTIONS]

  --pings        PATH   Pings parquet (required)
  --flagged      PATH   flagged.json (required)
  --output, -o   DIR    [./lostping_out]
```

---

## Data

Source: [Marine Cadastre (NOAA)](https://marinecadastre.gov/ais/) — free, no account needed.  
Format: daily `.csv.zst` files (Zstandard compressed), 2024 onwards.

```
mmsi, base_date_time, lon, lat, sog, cog, heading,
vessel_name, imo, call_sign, vessel_type, status,
length, width, draft, cargo, transceiver
```

Decompress with `zstd -d AIS_2024_01_03.csv.zst`.  
Gulf of Mexico zone recommended for first runs — good mix of tankers, cargo, and fishing vessels.

Optional boundary files (drop into `data/boundaries/`):

- EEZ shapefile — passed via `--eez`
- STS zone GeoJSON — passed via `--sts-zones` (five zones hardcoded by default: Gulf of Mexico, Strait of Hormuz, Gulf of Aden, East China Sea, Black Sea)

---

## Scoring

```python
risk = (0.40 * isolation_score
      + 0.35 * gap_score
      + 0.25 * loiter_score) * 100
```

| Signal | Module | Method |
|---|---|---|
| Trajectory anomaly | `isolation.py` | Isolation Forest per vessel type |
| AIS gap | `gaps.py` | Time-diff between pings + STS zone proximity |
| Loitering | `loiter.py` | DBSCAN spatial clustering |

A gap longer than 8 h gets a 1.3× severity multiplier. Scores are capped at 100.  
The `reason` field in `flagged.json` is a human-readable string explaining which signals fired and why.

